# secrets
.env
*.pem

# python
.venv/
# .venv-kg (build_kg.py's isolated scispacy/spacy env, see that module's
# docstring) was missing here entirely until verified directly against
# `du -sh` before this repo's first commit -- 356MB of compiled
# native/binary packages that were about to be staged wholesale.
.venv-kg/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# raw data snapshots (S3 is the system of record) -- **/*.json, not just
# the top-level *.json: verified directly (find data/raw -mindepth 2) that
# fetch_daily_updates.py's own bulk_seed/ and daily_delta/ subdirectories
# were NOT covered by the single-level glob this replaces, so real archived
# payloads were slipping through it. Also *.json.zip and *.md: caught by a
# `git add -A -n` dry-run before this repo's first commit actually staging
# an openFDA bulk_seed .json.zip archive and ingest_pipeline.py's parsed
# PDF .md output, neither of which the plain *.json pattern matches.
data/raw/**/*.json
data/raw/**/*.json.zip
data/raw/**/*.md

# transient run artifacts from this session's background seed/delta jobs
# (log + pid files from seed_bulk_data.py invocations) -- caught by the
# same pre-commit dry-run; operational output, not project source.
seed_*.log
seed_*.pid

# SEC EDGAR downloaded filings (fetch_sec_edgar.py) -- large (full-submission.txt
# alone measured 29.5MB for one real MRK 10-K) and reproducible any time via
# sec-edgar-downloader; never meant to be version-controlled, same reasoning
# as qdrant_storage/ and neo4j_data/ below.
data/raw/sec_edgar/

# node / Next.js
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/

# local database volumes -- bind-mounted Docker storage for Qdrant/Neo4j.
# Verified sizes before adding this (`du -sh`): qdrant_storage/ 4.8GB,
# neo4j_data/ 1.5GB at last check, growing with every bulk-seed run.
# Entirely reproducible from S3 + the seed/delta scripts; never meant to be
# version-controlled, and neither was covered here before this repo's
# first commit.
qdrant_storage/
neo4j_data/

# scratch output of migrate_snapshot.py-style one-off migrations (offline
# neo4j-admin dump used to seed AWS's Neo4j -- see terraform/main.tf's
# aws_lb.main idle_timeout comment for that migration's context). ~230MB,
# never meant to be version-controlled; the real copy lives in S3.
neo4j_dumps/

# os
.DS_Store

# local Claude Code session state (not project source)
.claude/

# terraform (state and .tfvars can both hold secret values / account details)
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored -- it pins provider
# versions and should be committed, same as a package-lock.json.
terraform/.terraform/
terraform/*.tfstate
terraform/*.tfstate.*
terraform/*.tfvars
terraform/crash.log

# pre-migration state backups (see .state-backups/ -- local safety copies
# made before `terraform init -migrate-state`, same reasoning as the
# terraform.tfstate* rules above: can hold real infrastructure details)
.state-backups/
